From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:33:54 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: derive MSB vs script string buffers from the buffer
 context

Upstreamable generic engine fix.

Several string consumers (SystemMes box, selection menu, clear list, tips
menu, tips list entries) set dummy.UseMSBBuffers from the global
Profile::Vm::UseMsbStrings. That misreads every string that is not in an
MSB buffer on a UseMsbStrings game, e.g. SystemMes modes without the 0x80
bit and SelectionMenu types 1/2, which use ScriptGetStrAddress.

The BufferOffsetContext already says which buffers the offset belongs to, so:
 - InstSel and InstSystemMes now fill ctx.Buffers (MsbBuffers for the 0x80
   forms, ScriptBuffers otherwise) instead of passing an empty span;
 - the consumers call dummy.SetStringIp(ctx), which derives the flag from
   the context (tips consumers build the context from
   TipsSystem::GetTipsScriptBufferCtx(), which already selects the buffers);
 - the PS3-style save entry and clear list play-time labels use
   SetStringIp(ctx) as well so all of them share one definition.

Behaviour for games without UseMsbStrings is unchanged (ScriptBuffers ->
non-MSB, as before). For the UseMsbStrings games (MO8, CHN, CC/CHLCC Switch)
the MSB forms are read exactly as before; the non-MSB forms of
SystemMes/Sel on the MO6TW SysMesBox and SelectionMenu paths are now read
from the script buffer instead of being misread as MSB. That is a
correctness fix toward the data layout, not a regression, but it is not
re-verified on those games' devices.

